Description: Python 3 interface to the Lab Streaming Layer
 The Lab Streaming Layer (LSL) is a system for unified collection of
 measurement time series in research experiments. pylsl is the Python
 interface to the LSL core library (liblsl): it lets Python programs push
 and pull multi-channel time series with built-in network transport and
 time synchronisation, widely used to acquire and synchronise EEG, eye
 tracking, motion capture and other data streams.
 .
 This package provides the ctypes binding; it uses the system liblsl
 shared library (liblsl2) at runtime.
